# Answer key for t5_metamorphic.sql - B1 core SELECT, metamorphic pairs + one realistic model.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
#
# Each pair's facts are listed ONCE, at spelling A's line: both spellings write the same
# target and claim the same facts, and a key cannot hold one fact twice. So the key scores
# whether the lineage is right; stress/pg/metamorphic.py scores whether B agrees with A.
# A spelling that is wrong in a way its twin is right shows up in the pair check even
# when the key is satisfied by the twin.

@ 28 P1 USING vs ON
value staging.shipments.order_id -> mart.top_customers.customer_id identity
value staging.shipments.carrier_id -> mart.top_customers.position identity
value staging.payments.amount -> mart.top_customers.revenue identity

@ 44 P2 named window vs inline
value core.fct_order_line.product_key -> mart.product_performance.product_id identity
value core.fct_order_line.net_amount -> mart.product_performance.running_revenue aggregated
influence core.fct_order_line.store_id, core.fct_order_line.order_date -> mart.product_performance.running_revenue

@ 59 P3 GROUP BY ordinals vs names
value core.dim_store.region -> mart.kpi_rollup.region identity
value core.dim_store.country_code -> mart.kpi_rollup.country_code identity
value core.fct_order_line.amount_usd -> mart.kpi_rollup.revenue aggregated
influence core.dim_store.region, core.dim_store.country_code -> mart.kpi_rollup.orders, mart.kpi_rollup.revenue

@ 77 P4 DISTINCT vs GROUP BY without aggregates
value staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix.channel identity
value staging.orders.currency -> mart.channel_mix.region identity
forbid filter staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix | DISTINCT / GROUP BY with no aggregate removes only duplicate written values (D-9)

@ 92 P5 ROLLUP vs the equivalent GROUPING SETS
value core.dim_customer.region -> mart.kpi_rollup.region identity
value core.dim_customer.segment -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity
value core.fct_order_line.net_amount -> mart.kpi_rollup.revenue aggregated
influence core.dim_customer.region, core.dim_customer.segment -> mart.kpi_rollup.revenue

@ 112 P6 HAVING vs WHERE over an aggregating subquery
value core.fct_order_line.store_id -> mart.sales_daily.store_id identity
value core.fct_order_line.net_amount -> mart.sales_daily.net_amount aggregated
influence core.fct_order_line.store_id -> mart.sales_daily.net_amount
filter core.fct_order_line.net_amount -> mart.sales_daily post

@ 133 P7 COUNT(DISTINCT x) vs COUNT(x) over SELECT DISTINCT
value staging.orders.customer_id -> mart.customer_summary.customer_id identity
value staging.orders.store_id -> mart.customer_summary.lifetime_orders aggregated
influence staging.orders.customer_id -> mart.customer_summary.lifetime_orders

@ 152 P8 FILTER vs CASE inside AVG (D-10)
value core.fct_shipment.carrier_id -> mart.carrier_scorecard.carrier_id identity
value core.fct_shipment.transit_days, core.fct_shipment.status -> mart.carrier_scorecard.avg_transit_days aggregated
influence core.fct_shipment.carrier_id -> mart.carrier_scorecard.avg_transit_days
forbid filter core.fct_shipment.status -> mart.carrier_scorecard | FILTER changes one aggregate's value, exactly as the CASE spelling does (D-10)

@ 168 P9 JOIN ON vs comma join (D-11)
value core.fct_order_line.order_date -> mart.sales_daily.sale_date identity
value core.dim_store.region -> mart.sales_daily.region identity
value core.fct_order_line.gross_amount -> mart.sales_daily.gross_amount identity
forbid filter core.fct_order_line.store_id -> mart.sales_daily | the join condition, whether written in ON or WHERE (D-5, D-11)
forbid filter core.dim_store.id -> mart.sales_daily | the join condition, whether written in ON or WHERE (D-5, D-11)

@ 184 P10 ROW_NUMBER() = 1 vs DISTINCT ON (D-9)
value staging.orders.customer_id -> mart.top_customers.customer_id identity
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.top_customers.revenue identity
filter staging.orders.customer_id, staging.orders.order_ts -> mart.top_customers
note D-9: in A the rank's PARTITION BY and ORDER BY decide which row survives `rn = 1`; in B the DISTINCT ON key and its tie-breaker do.

@ 212 R1 the customer summary model
value core.dim_customer.customer_id -> mart.customer_summary.customer_id identity
value core.dim_customer.full_name -> mart.customer_summary.full_name derived
value core.dim_customer.segment -> mart.customer_summary.segment derived
note COALESCE(segment, 'UNKNOWN'): one column argument, a null guard.
value core.dim_customer.region -> mart.customer_summary.region identity
value core.fct_order_line.order_date -> mart.customer_summary.first_order_date, mart.customer_summary.last_order_date aggregated
value core.fct_order_line.amount_usd -> mart.customer_summary.lifetime_value, mart.customer_summary.avg_basket aggregated
value core.fct_order_line.order_date -> mart.customer_summary.status aggregated
note status is a CASE over last_order = MAX(MIN(order_date)); the hardest construct on the path is the aggregate.
note lifetime_orders is COUNT(*) over order_facts: no value source. value_rank and value_decile are ranks: no value source.
influence core.fct_order_line.customer_key, core.fct_order_line.order_id -> mart.customer_summary.first_order_date, mart.customer_summary.last_order_date, mart.customer_summary.lifetime_value, mart.customer_summary.avg_basket, mart.customer_summary.status
note order_facts groups by (customer_key, order_id); customer_rollup groups by customer_key again. Both apply on every path through an aggregate of order_facts.
influence core.fct_order_line.customer_key, core.fct_order_line.order_id -> mart.customer_summary.lifetime_orders
note D-55 (2026-10-07): COUNT(*) counts order_facts' groups, so its GROUP BY order_id decides the count, as it decides every other aggregate here; relabelled from customer_key alone (FM-03).
influence core.dim_customer.region, core.fct_order_line.amount_usd, core.fct_order_line.customer_key, core.fct_order_line.order_id -> mart.customer_summary.value_rank
influence core.fct_order_line.amount_usd, core.fct_order_line.customer_key, core.fct_order_line.order_id -> mart.customer_summary.value_decile
filter core.fct_order_line.status -> mart.customer_summary
filter core.fct_order_line.amount_usd -> mart.customer_summary post
filter core.dim_customer.customer_id, core.dim_customer.valid_from -> mart.customer_summary
note D-9: the DISTINCT ON key and tie-breaker pick the current SCD row.
filter core.dim_customer.region -> mart.customer_summary
forbid value core.fct_order_line.amount_usd -> mart.customer_summary.value_rank | RANK orders by LTV; no part of LTV is in the rank (D-4)
forbid value core.fct_order_line.amount_usd -> mart.customer_summary.value_decile | NTILE orders by LTV; no part of LTV is in the decile (D-4)
forbid filter core.dim_customer.customer_key -> mart.customer_summary | the join between current_customer and customer_rollup is in ON (D-5)
forbid value core.fct_order_line.quantity -> mart.customer_summary.avg_basket | order_units is computed in order_facts and never read again
